                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_36">Battle,
                                Sussex, Benedictine abbey of St Martin</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval
                                Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the
                                Supplement (1987). On the corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                                Britain index card, Ker rejects the idea that Royal MS 8 D.xviii is
                                related to known Battle Abbey material (<ref
                                    target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_382">Cotton
                                    MS Tiberius B.v, fols. 2-73, 77-88</ref> + <ref
                                    target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_383">Cotton
                                    MS Nero D. ii, fols. 238-241</ref>). In his words, "The
                                connection with Tib. B. v and Nero D ii seems extremely
                                dubious."</p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">John, Lord
                                Lumley</persName></provenance>
